      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "topic:pivoting",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 60,
      "y": 440,
      "width": 1800,
      "height": 140,
      "text": "# Reach internal services\n\nStart from the pivot's current shell/process or accepted SSH access; another reachable subnet and an operational tunnel are not assumed.",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "flow:pivoting:home",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 60,
      "y": 620,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 240,
      "text": "## Investigation flow\n\nReach internal services\n\n · \n\nBranches describe evidence and missing conditions. Follow one useful lead, then return to unfinished coverage.",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "flow:pivoting:check-0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 560,
      "y": 620,
      "width": 760,
      "height": 348,
      "text": "## Enumerate what the pivot can actually reach\n\nRun route/listener checks on the pivot itself; do not infer its access from the attacker machine.\n\n```bash\nip addr\nip route\nss -lntup\n```\n\n**Discover pivot interfaces, routes and internal service context — on this canvas**"
    },
    {
      "id": "flow:pivoting:check-0-finding-0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1610,
      "y": 620,
      "width": 610,
      "height": 180,
      "text": "### One internal TCP endpoint is reachable from the pivot\n\nDraw the local/pivot listener and initiator before choosing a fixed forward.\n\n**Forward a selected service through an SSH client-side listener — on this canvas**",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "flow:pivoting:check-0-finding-1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1610,
      "y": 845,
      "width": 610,
      "height": 180,
      "text": "### Several internal services need proxy/routed access\n\nMatch the client protocol to SOCKS or a TUN route.\n\n**Provide SOCKS access through SSH dynamic forwarding — on this canvas**",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "flow:pivoting:check-0-fallback",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2380,
      "y": 620,
      "width": 610,
      "height": 180,
      "text": "### Unresolved / alternate check\n\nThe pivot cannot reach the destination: fix that leg before adding a tunnel.\n\n**Discover pivot interfaces, routes and internal service context — on this canvas**",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "flow:pivoting:check-1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 560,
      "y": 1250,
      "width": 760,
      "height": 396,
      "text": "## Use SSH forwarding for the required direction\n\nUse this when the attacker can SSH to a pivot that can reach the destination; remote forwarding reverses the listener placement.\n\n```bash\nssh -N \\\n  -L 127.0.0.1:LOCAL_PORT:INTERNAL_HOST:INTERNAL_PORT \\\n  -p SSH_PORT USER@PIVOT \\\n  -o ExitOnForwardFailure=yes \\\n  -o ServerAliveInterval=30 -o ServerAliveCountMax=3\n```\n\n**Forward a selected service through an SSH client-side listener — on this canvas**"
    },
    {
      "id": "flow:pivoting:check-1-finding-0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1610,
      "y": 1250,
      "width": 610,
      "height": 180,
      "text": "### The forwarded service responds through the listener\n\nRe-enumerate that destination with the matching service client.\n\n[[tracks/01 Discovery.canvas|Identify applications and validate selected NSE checks → 01 Discovery]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "flow:pivoting:check-1-finding-1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1610,
      "y": 1475,
      "width": 610,
      "height": 180,
      "text": "### Only the pivot can initiate the tunnel connection\n\nSelect the reverse/listener arrangement deliberately.\n\n**Expose an SSH-client-side destination through a server-side remote listener — on this canvas**",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "flow:pivoting:check-1-fallback",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2380,
      "y": 1250,
      "width": 610,
      "height": 204,
      "text": "### Unresolved / alternate check\n\nThe listener exists but the app fails: test destination reachability and DNS through the chosen path.\n\n**Preserve DNS, Kerberos names and time across a pivot — on this canvas**",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "flow:pivoting:check-2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 560,
      "y": 1880,
      "width": 760,
      "height": 300,
      "text": "## Use Ligolo for a justified routed requirement\n\nUse the version-specific agent/proxy procedure and route setup. A tunnel session alone is not a working destination route.\n\n```bash\n./proxy -selfcert -laddr 0.0.0.0:LIGOLO_PORT\n```\n\n**Route a selected internal subnet through Ligolo-ng — on this canvas**"
    },
    {
      "id": "flow:pivoting:check-2-finding-0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1610,
      "y": 1880,
      "width": 610,
      "height": 180,
      "text": "### The selected subnet is routed and the destination responds\n\nRe-run service discovery from that new position.\n\n[[tracks/01 Discovery.canvas|Identify applications and validate selected NSE checks → 01 Discovery]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "flow:pivoting:check-2-finding-1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1610,
      "y": 2105,
      "width": 610,
      "height": 180,
      "text": "### Delivery works but the payload callback fails\n\nBuild and verify the separately needed return/callback path.\n\n**Build the callback and delivery routes separately from the attack route — on this canvas**",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "flow:pivoting:check-2-fallback",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2380,
      "y": 1880,
      "width": 610,
      "height": 204,
      "text": "### Unresolved / alternate check\n\nRoute/session setup fails: inspect the route, interface privileges and each connection leg.\n\n**Discover pivot interfaces, routes and internal service context — on this canvas**",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "notes:pivoting",
      "type": "file",
      "file": "notes/pivoting.md",
      "x": 60,
      "y": 2515,
      "width": 2100,
      "height": 850
    },
    {
      "id": "notes-label:pivoting",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2350,
      "y": 2515,
      "width": 1400,
      "height": 180,
      "text": "## Full procedures and alternatives\n\nThe adjacent embedded note is readable here. Scroll inside it for complete variants. Commands and decisions continue below.",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:pivot-state:start",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 70,
      "y": 3790,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 250,
      "text": "## Discover pivot interfaces, routes and internal service context\n\nA foothold exposes an interface/subnet or a loopback-only service",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:pivot-state:discover",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 570,
      "y": 3750,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 228,
      "text": "### Discover\n\n```text\nip addr\nip route\nss -lntup\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:pivot-state:interpret",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1500,
      "y": 3730,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### What the output establishes\n\nA second network or loopback listener supplies a new vantage candidate; forwarding is not automatically enabled.",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:pivot-state:validate",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1500,
      "y": 3976,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 180,
      "text": "### Missing prerequisite\n\nRead interfaces/routes/listeners on the pivot and probe the internal destination from that host. Draw both legs and the initiator; only choose SSH/SOCKS/Ligolo after the destination leg works.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:pivot-state:enabled",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 3680,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Condition confirmed\n\nThe pivot reaches the needed endpoint and a supported tunnel can carry the client: choose that route.\n\n**Verify:** Record source, pivot, destination, protocol, listener placement and required return path.\n\n[[notes/pivoting.md#pivot-state|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:pivot-state:ruledout",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 4021,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 132,
      "text": "### Condition disproved here\n\nThe new subnet is outside assigned scope: do not use it as an attack route.",
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:pivot-state:unknown",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 4218,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 132,
      "text": "### Evidence inconclusive\n\nInterface/route presence alone does not prove destination/firewall access.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:pivot-state:action",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 3680,
      "width": 900,
      "height": 444,
      "text": "### Procedure entry — full sequence in the note\n\n```text\nAPPLICATION TOOL\n  -> local listener / SOCKS endpoint / TUN route\n  -> tunnel transport endpoint\n  -> pivot exit\n  -> internal destination service\n\nCALLBACK TARGET\n  -> pivot listener or routable address\n  -> relay/tunnel\n  -> final listener\n```\n\n[[notes/pivoting.md#pivot-state|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:pivot-state:next-0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 4214,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Relay a single TCP service through a fixed forward\n\n**When:** One reachable pivot can connect to one internal TCP destination\n\n**Still required:** A bindable pivot listener, source-to-listener access and pivot-to-destination connectivity\n\n**Relay a single TCP service through a fixed forward — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:pivot-state:next-1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 4521,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Forward a selected service through an SSH client-side listener\n\n**When:** SSH reaches a server that can access the needed internal service\n\n**Still required:** Accepted SSH identity and forwarding policy; local listener availability and SSH-server-to-destination route\n\n**Forward a selected service through an SSH client-side listener — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:pivot-state:next-2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 4828,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Use a reverse Chisel SOCKS or fixed TCP tunnel\n\n**When:** A pivot can make outbound HTTP/WebSocket connections to the tunnel server\n\n**Still required:** Compatible reviewed client/server, server reverse mode, reachable server port and pivot-to-destination access\n\n**Use a reverse Chisel SOCKS or fixed TCP tunnel — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:pivot-state:next-3",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 5159,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Route a selected internal subnet through Ligolo-ng\n\n**When:** Several protocols/subnets require a route-style interface through an agent\n\n**Still required:** Compatible proxy/agent, permitted local interface/route management, reachable carrier and selected assigned subnet\n\n**Route a selected internal subnet through Ligolo-ng — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:pivot-state:next-4",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 5490,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Expose a server-side SOCKS proxy through remote dynamic SSH forwarding\n\n**When:** Only the pivot can initiate SSH, but several client-selected internal destinations are needed\n\n**Still required:** A supporting OpenSSH client, allowed remote forwarding, listener binding and SOCKS-compatible tool clients\n\n**Expose a server-side SOCKS proxy through remote dynamic SSH forwarding — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:pivot-state:next-5",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 5821,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Route a selected subnet through sshuttle\n\n**When:** Multiple internal TCP destinations need transparent application access over SSH\n\n**Still required:** Working SSH/Python environment, local routing/firewall privileges and explicitly selected supported traffic/subnets\n\n**Route a selected subnet through sshuttle — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:pivot-state:next-6",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 6152,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Forward from Windows with OpenSSH, Plink or Netsh\n\n**When:** The pivot is Windows and available networking utilities constrain the route\n\n**Still required:** Compatible OpenSSH/Plink authentication or administrative Netsh/IP Helper context; correct listener and destination paths\n\n**Forward from Windows with OpenSSH, Plink or Netsh — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:pivot-state:next-7",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 6483,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Use forward Chisel SOCKS and version-supported UDP routing\n\n**When:** The assessment-side client can reach a pivot-side tunnel server\n\n**Still required:** Compatible client/server roles, reachable carrier, correctly placed SOCKS listener and explicitly supported UDP-aware mode when required\n\n**Use forward Chisel SOCKS and version-supported UDP routing — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:pivot-state:next-8",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 6814,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Compose multiple pivots and validate every connection leg\n\n**When:** A second internal network is reachable only from a later foothold\n\n**Still required:** A working first route, explicit second carrier/listener directions and correct per-hop DNS/return paths\n\n**Compose multiple pivots and validate every connection leg — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:fixed-forward:start",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 70,
      "y": 7421,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 250,
      "text": "## Relay a single TCP service through a fixed forward\n\nOne reachable pivot can connect to one internal TCP destination",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:fixed-forward:discover",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 570,
      "y": 7381,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 204,
      "text": "### Discover\n\n```text\nip route get TARGET\nss -lnt\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:fixed-forward:interpret",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1500,
      "y": 7361,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### What the output establishes\n\nA single TCP service can fit a fixed relay without assuming a full routed network.",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:fixed-forward:validate",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1500,
      "y": 7607,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Missing prerequisite\n\nConfirm both legs, bind address/permission and any additional dynamic ports or return path.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:fixed-forward:checks",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 570,
      "y": 7645,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Validate the condition\n\n```bash\nss -lnt\nip route get TARGET\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:fixed-forward:enabled",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 7311,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Condition confirmed\n\nBoth legs and the destination handshake work: choose a fixed TCP relay.\n\n**Verify:** Verify application behavior through the listener and keep the transport's destination explicit.\n\n[[notes/pivoting.md#fixed-forward|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:fixed-forward:ruledout",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 7628,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Condition disproved here\n\nThe protocol needs unprovided UDP or dynamic connections: reject this one-port topology.",
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:fixed-forward:unknown",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 7849,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Evidence inconclusive\n\nA listen socket without the destination handshake leaves the remote leg unknown.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:fixed-forward:action",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 7311,
      "width": 900,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Procedure entry — full sequence in the note\n\n```bash\nsocat -ddd TCP-LISTEN:LOCAL_PORT,bind=PIVOT_REACHABLE_IP,reuseaddr,fork \\\n  TCP:INTERNAL_HOST:INTERNAL_PORT\n```\n\n[[notes/pivoting.md#fixed-forward|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:fixed-forward:next-0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 7653,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Use SQL Server rights, impersonation and command facilities\n\n**When:** SQL Server credentials or a Windows identity accepted by the database\n\n**Still required:** Correct SQL versus Windows authentication; database role and configuration must permit the requested operation\n\n[[tracks/02 Services.canvas|Use SQL Server rights, impersonation and command facilities → 02 Services]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:fixed-forward:next-1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 7984,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Use MySQL/MariaDB data and file primitives\n\n**When:** A MySQL-compatible service and valid application/database credentials\n\n**Still required:** Database authentication and exact schema/file privileges; secure_file_priv and server filesystem identity constrain file actions\n\n[[tracks/02 Services.canvas|Use MySQL/MariaDB data and file primitives → 02 Services]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:fixed-forward:next-2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 8315,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Match route, destination service and effective authorization\n\n**When:** A credential appears valid but the destination's usable access is unknown\n\n**Still required:** Real source-to-service route, correct identity context and protocol-specific execution/logon rights\n\n[[tracks/09 Active Directory.canvas|Match route, destination service and effective authorization → 09 Active Directory]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ssh-local:start",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 70,
      "y": 8946,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 250,
      "text": "## Forward a selected service through an SSH client-side listener\n\nSSH reaches a server that can access the needed internal service",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ssh-local:discover",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 570,
      "y": 8906,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 204,
      "text": "### Discover\n\n```text\nssh -v -p SSH_PORT USER@PIVOT\nss -lnt\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ssh-local:interpret",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1500,
      "y": 8886,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### What the output establishes\n\nClient-side listener plus server-side destination is the -L direction; destination loopback belongs to the SSH server.",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ssh-local:validate",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1500,
      "y": 9132,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Missing prerequisite\n\nVerify forwarding policy, local bind and server-to-destination application access.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ssh-local:enabled",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 8836,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Condition confirmed\n\nThe permitted local forward delivers the service handshake: choose -L.\n\n**Verify:** Verify listening address plus the destination application's handshake and preserve correct hostname/SPN semantics when needed.\n\n[[notes/pivoting.md#ssh-local|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ssh-local:ruledout",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 9153,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Condition disproved here\n\nThe server cannot reach the selected destination: reject this topology regardless of valid SSH login.",
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ssh-local:unknown",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 9374,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 132,
      "text": "### Evidence inconclusive\n\nSSH login alone leaves forwarding policy unknown.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ssh-local:action",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 8836,
      "width": 900,
      "height": 324,
      "text": "### Procedure entry — full sequence in the note\n\n```bash\nssh -N \\\n  -L 127.0.0.1:LOCAL_PORT:INTERNAL_HOST:INTERNAL_PORT \\\n  -p SSH_PORT USER@PIVOT \\\n  -o ExitOnForwardFailure=yes \\\n  -o ServerAliveInterval=30 -o ServerAliveCountMax=3\n```\n\n[[notes/pivoting.md#ssh-local|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ssh-local:next-0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 9250,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Use MySQL/MariaDB data and file primitives\n\n**When:** A MySQL-compatible service and valid application/database credentials\n\n**Still required:** Database authentication and exact schema/file privileges; secure_file_priv and server filesystem identity constrain file actions\n\n[[tracks/02 Services.canvas|Use MySQL/MariaDB data and file primitives → 02 Services]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ssh-local:next-1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 9581,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Use SQL Server rights, impersonation and command facilities\n\n**When:** SQL Server credentials or a Windows identity accepted by the database\n\n**Still required:** Correct SQL versus Windows authentication; database role and configuration must permit the requested operation\n\n[[tracks/02 Services.canvas|Use SQL Server rights, impersonation and command facilities → 02 Services]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ssh-local:next-2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 9912,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Preserve DNS, Kerberos names and time across a pivot\n\n**When:** An IP connection works while hostname/Kerberos access fails\n\n**Still required:** Reachable correct resolver/KDC path, matching target SPN/hostname, realm configuration and acceptable time\n\n**Preserve DNS, Kerberos names and time across a pivot — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ssh-dynamic:start",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 70,
      "y": 10519,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 250,
      "text": "## Provide SOCKS access through SSH dynamic forwarding\n\nSeveral internal TCP services need access through one SSH server",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ssh-dynamic:discover",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 570,
      "y": 10479,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 180,
      "text": "### Discover\n\n```text\nssh -v -p SSH_PORT USER@PIVOT\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ssh-dynamic:interpret",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1500,
      "y": 10459,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### What the output establishes\n\nMultiple client-selected TCP destinations suggest a dynamic SOCKS listener rather than many fixed forwards.",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ssh-dynamic:validate",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1500,
      "y": 10705,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Missing prerequisite\n\nCheck SSH forwarding, listener bind, native/intercepted client support and DNS resolution location.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ssh-dynamic:enabled",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 10409,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Condition confirmed\n\nProxy-aware clients reach the selected applications: choose dynamic SOCKS.\n\n**Verify:** Verify one application through the proxy, then check each client's actual proxy and DNS behavior.\n\n[[notes/pivoting.md#ssh-dynamic|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ssh-dynamic:ruledout",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 10726,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Condition disproved here\n\nThe needed operation relies on raw/unsupported UDP traffic: reject ordinary TCP SOCKS for that operation.",
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ssh-dynamic:unknown",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 10947,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Evidence inconclusive\n\nA working SSH session without a proxy-aware test leaves application/proxy compatibility unknown.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ssh-dynamic:action",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 10409,
      "width": 900,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Procedure entry — full sequence in the note\n\n```bash\nssh -N -D 127.0.0.1:1080 -p SSH_PORT USER@PIVOT \\\n  -o ExitOnForwardFailure=yes \\\n  -o ServerAliveInterval=30 -o ServerAliveCountMax=3\n```\n\n[[notes/pivoting.md#ssh-dynamic|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ssh-dynamic:next-0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 10775,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Use ProxyChains, native SOCKS clients and SSH jump paths appropriately\n\n**When:** A SOCKS listener or an SSH jump host is already available\n\n**Still required:** Client/proxy transport compatibility, correct proxy configuration and controlled name resolution\n\n**Use ProxyChains, native SOCKS clients and SSH jump paths appropriately — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ssh-dynamic:next-1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 11082,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Discover TCP ports with SYN or connect scans\n\n**When:** An assigned host needs an initial service queue or full TCP coverage\n\n**Still required:** SYN scanning needs raw-packet privileges; connect scanning needs OS TCP connections; specify selected versus full port coverage\n\n[[tracks/01 Discovery.canvas|Discover TCP ports with SYN or connect scans → 01 Discovery]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ssh-dynamic:next-2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 11413,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Preserve DNS, Kerberos names and time across a pivot\n\n**When:** An IP connection works while hostname/Kerberos access fails\n\n**Still required:** Reachable correct resolver/KDC path, matching target SPN/hostname, realm configuration and acceptable time\n\n**Preserve DNS, Kerberos names and time across a pivot — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ssh-remote:start",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 70,
      "y": 12020,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 250,
      "text": "## Expose an SSH-client-side destination through a server-side remote listener\n\nThe useful side can initiate SSH outward but cannot accept an inbound management connection",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ssh-remote:discover",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 570,
      "y": 11980,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 180,
      "text": "### Discover\n\n```text\nssh -v USER@SSH_SERVER\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ssh-remote:interpret",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1500,
      "y": 11960,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### What the output establishes\n\nThe useful listener is on the SSH server while the destination is reached from the client side: a remote forward candidate.",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ssh-remote:validate",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1500,
      "y": 12206,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Missing prerequisite\n\nVerify remote-forward permission, server bind/GatewayPorts policy and pivot-side destination reachability.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ssh-remote:checks",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 570,
      "y": 12220,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Validate the condition\n\n```bash\nssh -v USER@SSH_SERVER\nss -lnt\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ssh-remote:enabled",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 11910,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Condition confirmed\n\nThe server-side listener carries the intended service: choose the -R fixed forward.\n\n**Verify:** Verify listener placement/bind and actual destination application response.\n\n[[notes/pivoting.md#ssh-remote|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ssh-remote:ruledout",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 12251,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Condition disproved here\n\nOnly a loopback listener is available but another host must connect and no approved bind path exists: reject that exposure design.",
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ssh-remote:unknown",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 12472,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 132,
      "text": "### Evidence inconclusive\n\nAccepted outbound SSH does not prove remote listener policy.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ssh-remote:action",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 11910,
      "width": 900,
      "height": 324,
      "text": "### Procedure entry — full sequence in the note\n\n```bash\nssh -N \\\n  -R 127.0.0.1:KALI_PORT:INTERNAL_HOST:INTERNAL_PORT \\\n  -p KALI_SSH_PORT KALI_USER@LHOST \\\n  -o ExitOnForwardFailure=yes \\\n  -o ServerAliveInterval=30 -o ServerAliveCountMax=3\n```\n\n[[notes/pivoting.md#ssh-remote|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ssh-remote:next-0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 12324,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Match route, destination service and effective authorization\n\n**When:** A credential appears valid but the destination's usable access is unknown\n\n**Still required:** Real source-to-service route, correct identity context and protocol-specific execution/logon rights\n\n[[tracks/09 Active Directory.canvas|Match route, destination service and effective authorization → 09 Active Directory]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ssh-remote:next-1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 12655,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Enumerate SMB/RPC shares, files and identities\n\n**When:** SMB/RPC endpoints, domain clues or new credentials\n\n**Still required:** Reachable SMB/RPC; anonymous, guest, local or domain context must be explicit; share and filesystem ACLs both matter\n\n[[tracks/02 Services.canvas|Enumerate SMB/RPC shares, files and identities → 02 Services]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ssh-remote:next-2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 12962,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Build the callback and delivery routes separately from the attack route\n\n**When:** A pivoted exploit reaches its target but its shell/download cannot return\n\n**Still required:** Target-to-listener/download-server path, correct advertised address and compatible reverse listener/forward\n\n**Build the callback and delivery routes separately from the attack route — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ssh-remote-dynamic:start",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 70,
      "y": 13593,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 250,
      "text": "## Expose a server-side SOCKS proxy through remote dynamic SSH forwarding\n\nOnly the pivot can initiate SSH, but several client-selected internal destinations are needed",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ssh-remote-dynamic:discover",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 570,
      "y": 13553,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 180,
      "text": "### Discover\n\n```text\nssh -V\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ssh-remote-dynamic:interpret",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1500,
      "y": 13533,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### What the output establishes\n\nRemote listener placement plus per-connection SOCKS destination selection suggests remote dynamic forwarding.",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ssh-remote-dynamic:validate",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1500,
      "y": 13779,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Missing prerequisite\n\nCheck implementation support, remote-forward policy, listener binding and proxy-client/DNS compatibility.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ssh-remote-dynamic:enabled",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 13483,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Condition confirmed\n\nA supported remote dynamic listener carries the intended TCP clients: choose that mode.\n\n**Verify:** Verify the listener's actual location and source-side exit by application evidence.\n\n[[notes/pivoting.md#ssh-remote-dynamic|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ssh-remote-dynamic:ruledout",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 13824,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Condition disproved here\n\nThe installed SSH client does not support the syntax or policy forbids it: reject that variant.",
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ssh-remote-dynamic:unknown",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 14045,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Evidence inconclusive\n\nA version string without a controlled forwarding/application test leaves policy/transport unresolved.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ssh-remote-dynamic:action",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 13483,
      "width": 900,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Procedure entry — full sequence in the note\n\n```bash\nssh -N -R 127.0.0.1:1080 -p KALI_SSH_PORT KALI_USER@LHOST \\\n  -o ExitOnForwardFailure=yes \\\n  -o ServerAliveInterval=30 -o ServerAliveCountMax=3\n```\n\n[[notes/pivoting.md#ssh-remote-dynamic|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ssh-remote-dynamic:next-0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 13849,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Use ProxyChains, native SOCKS clients and SSH jump paths appropriately\n\n**When:** A SOCKS listener or an SSH jump host is already available\n\n**Still required:** Client/proxy transport compatibility, correct proxy configuration and controlled name resolution\n\n**Use ProxyChains, native SOCKS clients and SSH jump paths appropriately — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ssh-remote-dynamic:next-1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 14156,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 300,
      "text": "### Expose an SSH-client-side destination through a server-side remote listener\n\n**When:** The useful side can initiate SSH outward but cannot accept an inbound management connection\n\n**Still required:** Outbound SSH route, accepted identity, server forwarding/GatewayPorts policy and reachability to the chosen client-side destination\n\n**Expose an SSH-client-side destination through a server-side remote listener — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ssh-remote-dynamic:next-2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
