      "text": "### Preserve DNS, Kerberos names and time across a pivot\n\n**When:** An IP connection works while hostname/Kerberos access fails\n\n**Still required:** Reachable correct resolver/KDC path, matching target SPN/hostname, realm configuration and acceptable time\n\n**Preserve DNS, Kerberos names and time across a pivot — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:proxy-clients:start",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 70,
      "y": 15118,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 250,
      "text": "## Use ProxyChains, native SOCKS clients and SSH jump paths appropriately\n\nA SOCKS listener or an SSH jump host is already available",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:proxy-clients:discover",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 570,
      "y": 15078,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 180,
      "text": "### Discover\n\n```text\ncurl --socks5-hostname 127.0.0.1:SOCKS_PORT http://TARGET:PORT/\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:proxy-clients:interpret",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1500,
      "y": 15058,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### What the output establishes\n\nOne supported TCP application works; the proxy does not automatically carry raw packets or arbitrary DNS/UDP.",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:proxy-clients:validate",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1500,
      "y": 15304,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Missing prerequisite\n\nCheck native versus intercepted support, connect-only scanner modes, name resolution and every required protocol leg.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:proxy-clients:enabled",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 15008,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Condition confirmed\n\nThe actual client's application handshake works through the chosen proxy/jump: use it.\n\n**Verify:** Verify destination application and resolver behavior through the intended path.\n\n[[notes/pivoting.md#proxy-clients|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:proxy-clients:ruledout",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 15349,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Condition disproved here\n\nA static/raw/UDP-only client is incompatible with this proxy wrapper: choose another transport.",
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:proxy-clients:unknown",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 15570,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Evidence inconclusive\n\nA reachable SOCKS port without an end-to-end service test leaves the exit path unknown.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:proxy-clients:action",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 15008,
      "width": 900,
      "height": 228,
      "text": "### Procedure entry — full sequence in the note\n\n```bash\nssh -J PIVOT_USER@PIVOT TARGET_USER@INTERNAL_HOST\n```\n\n[[notes/pivoting.md#proxy-clients|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:proxy-clients:next-0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 15326,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Discover TCP ports with SYN or connect scans\n\n**When:** An assigned host needs an initial service queue or full TCP coverage\n\n**Still required:** SYN scanning needs raw-packet privileges; connect scanning needs OS TCP connections; specify selected versus full port coverage\n\n[[tracks/01 Discovery.canvas|Discover TCP ports with SYN or connect scans → 01 Discovery]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:proxy-clients:next-1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 15657,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Match route, destination service and effective authorization\n\n**When:** A credential appears valid but the destination's usable access is unknown\n\n**Still required:** Real source-to-service route, correct identity context and protocol-specific execution/logon rights\n\n[[tracks/09 Active Directory.canvas|Match route, destination service and effective authorization → 09 Active Directory]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:proxy-clients:next-2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 15988,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Route a selected internal subnet through Ligolo-ng\n\n**When:** Several protocols/subnets require a route-style interface through an agent\n\n**Still required:** Compatible proxy/agent, permitted local interface/route management, reachable carrier and selected assigned subnet\n\n**Route a selected internal subnet through Ligolo-ng — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:sshuttle-route:start",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 70,
      "y": 16619,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 250,
      "text": "## Route a selected subnet through sshuttle\n\nMultiple internal TCP destinations need transparent application access over SSH",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:sshuttle-route:discover",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 570,
      "y": 16579,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 228,
      "text": "### Discover\n\n```text\nssh -v USER@PIVOT\npython3 --version\nip route\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:sshuttle-route:interpret",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1500,
      "y": 16559,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 180,
      "text": "### What the output establishes\n\nAn SSH carrier and compatible endpoints make a transparent selected-subnet route a candidate; local Python output alone does not prove the remote runtime.",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:sshuttle-route:validate",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1500,
      "y": 16829,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Missing prerequisite\n\nVerify local route/firewall permissions, remote runtime, supported transport/mode and explicitly selected subnet/DNS behavior.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:sshuttle-route:checks",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 570,
      "y": 16867,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Validate the condition\n\n```bash\nssh -v USER@PIVOT\npython3 --version\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:sshuttle-route:enabled",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 16509,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Condition confirmed\n\nThe selected application traffic works through the compatible mode: choose sshuttle.\n\n**Verify:** Verify the actual application path and ensure only assigned subnets are selected.\n\n[[notes/pivoting.md#sshuttle-route|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:sshuttle-route:ruledout",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 16850,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Condition disproved here\n\nRequired local permission or remote support is unavailable: reject this route implementation.",
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:sshuttle-route:unknown",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 17071,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Evidence inconclusive\n\nTCP success does not establish unsupported UDP/raw behavior; test the actual requirement.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:sshuttle-route:action",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 16509,
      "width": 900,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Procedure entry — full sequence in the note\n\n```bash\nsudo sshuttle --dns \\\n  -r SSH_USER@PIVOT:SSH_PORT \\\n  INTERNAL_SUBNET ANOTHER_SUBNET\n```\n\n[[notes/pivoting.md#sshuttle-route|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:sshuttle-route:next-0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 16875,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Preserve DNS, Kerberos names and time across a pivot\n\n**When:** An IP connection works while hostname/Kerberos access fails\n\n**Still required:** Reachable correct resolver/KDC path, matching target SPN/hostname, realm configuration and acceptable time\n\n**Preserve DNS, Kerberos names and time across a pivot — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:sshuttle-route:next-1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 17182,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Match route, destination service and effective authorization\n\n**When:** A credential appears valid but the destination's usable access is unknown\n\n**Still required:** Real source-to-service route, correct identity context and protocol-specific execution/logon rights\n\n[[tracks/09 Active Directory.canvas|Match route, destination service and effective authorization → 09 Active Directory]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:sshuttle-route:next-2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 17513,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Provide SOCKS access through SSH dynamic forwarding\n\n**When:** Several internal TCP services need access through one SSH server\n\n**Still required:** SSH forwarding allowed and clients that support SOCKS or compatible interception; DNS behavior must be chosen explicitly\n\n**Provide SOCKS access through SSH dynamic forwarding — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:windows-forward:start",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 70,
      "y": 18120,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 250,
      "text": "## Forward from Windows with OpenSSH, Plink or Netsh\n\nThe pivot is Windows and available networking utilities constrain the route",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:windows-forward:discover",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 570,
      "y": 18080,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 228,
      "text": "### Discover\n\n```text\nGet-Command ssh,plink,netsh -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue\nGet-Service iphlpsvc\nTest-NetConnection TARGET -Port PORT\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:windows-forward:interpret",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1500,
      "y": 18060,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### What the output establishes\n\nWindows has a carrier/destination candidate; Netsh administrative state and user-space SSH requirements differ.",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:windows-forward:validate",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1500,
      "y": 18306,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Missing prerequisite\n\nChoose the supported tool, verify listener/bind/firewall and correct connection direction; check its exact rights.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:windows-forward:enabled",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 18010,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Condition confirmed\n\nThe selected implementation carries the application and cleanup state is known: use it.\n\n**Verify:** Verify actual listener, route and application, then remove created portproxy/firewall state as appropriate.\n\n[[notes/pivoting.md#windows-forward|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:windows-forward:ruledout",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 18351,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Condition disproved here\n\nNo admin rights for portproxy rules out that Netsh route, not a valid user-space SSH option.",
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:windows-forward:unknown",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 18572,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Evidence inconclusive\n\nA running IP Helper service alone does not establish permission or a working forward.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:windows-forward:action",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 18010,
      "width": 900,
      "height": 300,
      "text": "### Procedure entry — full sequence in the note\n\n```cmd\nwhere ssh.exe\nssh.exe -V\nssh.exe -N -R 127.0.0.1:1080 KALI_USER@LHOST -p KALI_SSH_PORT -o ExitOnForwardFailure=yes -o ServerAliveInterval=30\n```\n\n[[notes/pivoting.md#windows-forward|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:windows-forward:next-0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 18400,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Match route, destination service and effective authorization\n\n**When:** A credential appears valid but the destination's usable access is unknown\n\n**Still required:** Real source-to-service route, correct identity context and protocol-specific execution/logon rights\n\n[[tracks/09 Active Directory.canvas|Match route, destination service and effective authorization → 09 Active Directory]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:windows-forward:next-1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 18731,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Forward a selected service through an SSH client-side listener\n\n**When:** SSH reaches a server that can access the needed internal service\n\n**Still required:** Accepted SSH identity and forwarding policy; local listener availability and SSH-server-to-destination route\n\n**Forward a selected service through an SSH client-side listener — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:windows-forward:next-2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 19038,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Build the callback and delivery routes separately from the attack route\n\n**When:** A pivoted exploit reaches its target but its shell/download cannot return\n\n**Still required:** Target-to-listener/download-server path, correct advertised address and compatible reverse listener/forward\n\n**Build the callback and delivery routes separately from the attack route — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:chisel-reverse:start",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 70,
      "y": 19669,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 250,
      "text": "## Use a reverse Chisel SOCKS or fixed TCP tunnel\n\nA pivot can make outbound HTTP/WebSocket connections to the tunnel server",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:chisel-reverse:discover",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 570,
      "y": 19629,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 228,
      "text": "### Discover\n\n```text\nchisel --version\nchisel server --help\nchisel client --help\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:chisel-reverse:interpret",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1500,
      "y": 19609,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### What the output establishes\n\nThe outbound carrier and server-side listener requirement identify a reverse-tunnel topology.",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:chisel-reverse:validate",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1500,
      "y": 19855,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Missing prerequisite\n\nVerify server reverse mode, fingerprint, carrier upgrade, listener bind and pivot-to-destination compatibility.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:chisel-reverse:enabled",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 19559,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Condition confirmed\n\nThe carrier and intended service handshake succeed: choose the matching reverse remote.\n\n**Verify:** Verify tunnel establishment and end-to-end application behavior; a connected carrier alone is insufficient.\n\n[[notes/pivoting.md#chisel-reverse|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:chisel-reverse:ruledout",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 19900,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Condition disproved here\n\nThe carrier/upgrade is blocked with no permitted route: reject this tunnel path.",
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:chisel-reverse:unknown",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 20121,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Evidence inconclusive\n\nA connected carrier without application response leaves listener/exit/client behavior unknown.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:chisel-reverse:action",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 19559,
      "width": 900,
      "height": 228,
      "text": "### Procedure entry — full sequence in the note\n\n```bash\nchisel server --reverse --port CHISEL_PORT\n```\n\n[[notes/pivoting.md#chisel-reverse|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:chisel-reverse:next-0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 19877,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Use ProxyChains, native SOCKS clients and SSH jump paths appropriately\n\n**When:** A SOCKS listener or an SSH jump host is already available\n\n**Still required:** Client/proxy transport compatibility, correct proxy configuration and controlled name resolution\n\n**Use ProxyChains, native SOCKS clients and SSH jump paths appropriately — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:chisel-reverse:next-1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 20184,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Match route, destination service and effective authorization\n\n**When:** A credential appears valid but the destination's usable access is unknown\n\n**Still required:** Real source-to-service route, correct identity context and protocol-specific execution/logon rights\n\n[[tracks/09 Active Directory.canvas|Match route, destination service and effective authorization → 09 Active Directory]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:chisel-reverse:next-2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 20515,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Preserve DNS, Kerberos names and time across a pivot\n\n**When:** An IP connection works while hostname/Kerberos access fails\n\n**Still required:** Reachable correct resolver/KDC path, matching target SPN/hostname, realm configuration and acceptable time\n\n**Preserve DNS, Kerberos names and time across a pivot — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:chisel-forward:start",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 70,
      "y": 21122,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 250,
      "text": "## Use forward Chisel SOCKS and version-supported UDP routing\n\nThe assessment-side client can reach a pivot-side tunnel server",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:chisel-forward:discover",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 570,
      "y": 21082,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 204,
      "text": "### Discover\n\n```text\nchisel --version\nchisel client --help\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:chisel-forward:interpret",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1500,
      "y": 21062,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### What the output establishes\n\nForward placement and actual client transport determine the mode; a UDP-capable tunnel binary does not make every wrapper UDP-capable.",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:chisel-forward:validate",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1500,
      "y": 21308,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Missing prerequisite\n\nVerify compatible peers, server SOCKS setting, listener route and the real application's UDP/TCP support.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:chisel-forward:enabled",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 21012,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Condition confirmed\n\nThe intended application's required transport works end to end: use that configured mode.\n\n**Verify:** Verify the actual required transport end to end, with correct listener/exit placement.\n\n[[notes/pivoting.md#chisel-forward|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:chisel-forward:ruledout",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 21353,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 132,
      "text": "### Condition disproved here\n\nA TCP-only wrapper is used for a UDP-only operation: reject that combination.",
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:chisel-forward:unknown",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 21550,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 132,
      "text": "### Evidence inconclusive\n\nTCP success without UDP-aware client/firewall evidence leaves UDP unresolved.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:chisel-forward:action",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 21012,
      "width": 900,
      "height": 348,
      "text": "### Procedure entry — full sequence in the note\n\n```bash\n# Pivot/server side\nchisel server --socks5 --port CHISEL_PORT\n\n# Kali/client side\nchisel client --fingerprint 'SERVER_FINGERPRINT' PIVOT:CHISEL_PORT \\\n  127.0.0.1:1080:socks\n```\n\n[[notes/pivoting.md#chisel-forward|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:chisel-forward:next-0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 21450,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Route a selected internal subnet through Ligolo-ng\n\n**When:** Several protocols/subnets require a route-style interface through an agent\n\n**Still required:** Compatible proxy/agent, permitted local interface/route management, reachable carrier and selected assigned subnet\n\n**Route a selected internal subnet through Ligolo-ng — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:chisel-forward:next-1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 21781,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Use ProxyChains, native SOCKS clients and SSH jump paths appropriately\n\n**When:** A SOCKS listener or an SSH jump host is already available\n\n**Still required:** Client/proxy transport compatibility, correct proxy configuration and controlled name resolution\n\n**Use ProxyChains, native SOCKS clients and SSH jump paths appropriately — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:chisel-forward:next-2",
