      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ligolo-route:next-2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 23541,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Build the callback and delivery routes separately from the attack route\n\n**When:** A pivoted exploit reaches its target but its shell/download cannot return\n\n**Still required:** Target-to-listener/download-server path, correct advertised address and compatible reverse listener/forward\n\n**Build the callback and delivery routes separately from the attack route — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:pivot-dns:start",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 70,
      "y": 24172,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 250,
      "text": "## Preserve DNS, Kerberos names and time across a pivot\n\nAn IP connection works while hostname/Kerberos access fails",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:pivot-dns:discover",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 570,
      "y": 24132,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 228,
      "text": "### Discover\n\n```text\ngetent hosts TARGET_HOST\nklist\ndate -u\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:pivot-dns:interpret",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1500,
      "y": 24112,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 132,
      "text": "### What the output establishes\n\nThe route and credential may be valid while name/SPN context is wrong.",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:pivot-dns:validate",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1500,
      "y": 24334,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Missing prerequisite\n\nCheck intended DNS source/result, realm/service name, time and KDC/service routes separately.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:pivot-dns:enabled",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 24062,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Condition confirmed\n\nCorrect naming/time and routes produce accepted service authentication: use that identity-preserving path.\n\n**Verify:** Verify resolved destination, ticket/server principal and actual authenticated application action.\n\n[[notes/pivoting.md#pivot-dns|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:pivot-dns:ruledout",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 24403,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 132,
      "text": "### Condition disproved here\n\nThe ticket names another service/host: reject it for this operation.",
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:pivot-dns:unknown",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 24600,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Evidence inconclusive\n\nSuccessful IP transport without named service evidence does not settle Kerberos.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:pivot-dns:action",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 24062,
      "width": 900,
      "height": 300,
      "text": "### Procedure entry — full sequence in the note\n\n```bash\ngetent hosts INTERNAL_FQDN\ncurl --socks5-hostname 127.0.0.1:1080 http://INTERNAL_FQDN:PORT/\nklist\nKRB5_TRACE=/dev/stderr kvno cifs/TARGET_HOST\n```\n\n[[notes/pivoting.md#pivot-dns|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:pivot-dns:next-0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 24452,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Inventory, convert and import tickets in the correct logon context\n\n**When:** A valid ticket/cache or a long-term key that can request a TGT\n\n**Still required:** Matching client/realm/service, valid lifetime, compatible format and available KDC/service routes; ticket import affects a specific context\n\n[[tracks/09 Active Directory.canvas|Inventory, convert and import tickets in the correct logon context → 09 Active Directory]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:pivot-dns:next-1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 24783,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Select password, NT hash, key-to-ticket or ticket authentication\n\n**When:** A password, actual NT hash, AES/NT long-term key or ticket is available\n\n**Still required:** Credential type accepted by the chosen protocol/client, correct identity/domain, naming/time and destination authorization\n\n[[tracks/09 Active Directory.canvas|Select password, NT hash, key-to-ticket or ticket authentication → 09 Active Directory]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:pivot-dns:next-2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 25114,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Establish domain identity, DC, DNS, time and route\n\n**When:** Domain credentials or a domain-joined foothold\n\n**Still required:** Correct realm/domain and account qualification; reachable DC/services, usable DNS and acceptable clock skew\n\n[[tracks/09 Active Directory.canvas|Establish domain identity, DC, DNS, time and route → 09 Active Directory]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:pivot-dns:next-3",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 25421,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Conditional: tunnel through controlled DNS infrastructure\n\n**When:** DNS is an available carrier while simpler permitted routes are unavailable\n\n**Still required:** Controlled/delegated domain or supported direct setup, reachable DNS path, compatible server/client and allowed execution\n\n**Conditional: tunnel through controlled DNS infrastructure — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:pivot-callback:start",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 70,
      "y": 26052,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 250,
      "text": "## Build the callback and delivery routes separately from the attack route\n\nA pivoted exploit reaches its target but its shell/download cannot return",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:pivot-callback:discover",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 570,
      "y": 26012,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 204,
      "text": "### Discover\n\n```text\nss -lnt\nip route get TARGET\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:pivot-callback:interpret",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1500,
      "y": 25992,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### What the output establishes\n\nA working initiating proxy path does not route a target's new connection back to that private interface.",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:pivot-callback:validate",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1500,
      "y": 26238,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Missing prerequisite\n\nCheck the target's route, listener bind, chosen reverse forward/agent listener and final handler.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:pivot-callback:enabled",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 25942,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Condition confirmed\n\nThe target-initiated leg reaches the intended receiver and effect is verified: use the return route.\n\n**Verify:** Verify the target-initiated connection from its source context and the final session or downloaded bytes.\n\n[[notes/pivoting.md#pivot-callback|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:pivot-callback:ruledout",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 26283,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Condition disproved here\n\nThe target cannot reach the advertised address and no selected forward provides it: reject that callback address/design.",
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:pivot-callback:unknown",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 26504,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Evidence inconclusive\n\nNo packets without execution proof leaves trigger and route separately unresolved.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:pivot-callback:action",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 25942,
      "width": 900,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Procedure entry — full sequence in the note\n\n```text\nKali -> tunnel -> internal service       # access path\ninternal target -> pivot -> Kali listener # callback path\n```\n\n[[notes/pivoting.md#pivot-callback|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:pivot-callback:next-0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 26284,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Diagnose connection direction, listener and session failures in order\n\n**When:** Command execution or payload delivery exists but the expected usable channel does not\n\n**Still required:** A recorded first execution proof, correct advertised route, active compatible listener and observable connection evidence\n\n[[tracks/11 Execution Troubleshooting.canvas|Diagnose connection direction, listener and session failures in order → 11 Execution Troubleshooting]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:pivot-callback:next-1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 26615,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Connect a Linux reverse shell through an available interpreter\n\n**When:** Linux command execution exists but an interactive channel is needed\n\n**Still required:** A confirmed Bash/Python/PHP/Netcat implementation, correct parser wrapping, target-to-listener route and compatible listener\n\n[[tracks/06 Shells and Transfers.canvas|Connect a Linux reverse shell through an available interpreter → 06 Shells and Transfers]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:pivot-callback:next-2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 26922,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Transfer over HTTP using Linux or Windows clients\n\n**When:** A tool/artifact must reach a target that can make an HTTP request\n\n**Still required:** Correct server bind and served directory; target-to-server route, available downloader and writable destination\n\n[[tracks/06 Shells and Transfers.canvas|Transfer over HTTP using Linux or Windows clients → 06 Shells and Transfers]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:pivot-multihop:start",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 70,
      "y": 27529,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 250,
      "text": "## Compose multiple pivots and validate every connection leg\n\nA second internal network is reachable only from a later foothold",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:pivot-multihop:discover",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 570,
      "y": 27489,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 228,
      "text": "### Discover\n\n```text\nhostname\nip route\nss -lnt\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:pivot-multihop:interpret",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1500,
      "y": 27469,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### What the output establishes\n\nThe break lies beyond a known working leg; a connected second carrier is not a complete final route.",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:pivot-multihop:validate",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1500,
      "y": 27715,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Missing prerequisite\n\nTest each listener-to-destination leg, names and return traffic independently from the correct source.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:pivot-multihop:checks",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 570,
      "y": 27777,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Validate the condition\n\n```bash\nip route\nss -lnt\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:pivot-multihop:enabled",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 27419,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Condition confirmed\n\nEvery required application leg is verified: use the composed route.\n\n**Verify:** Validate each hop with an application-aware test before chaining the final client.\n\n[[notes/pivoting.md#pivot-multihop|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:pivot-multihop:ruledout",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 27736,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Condition disproved here\n\nOne required hop cannot reach the destination under the selected topology: reject that composition.",
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:pivot-multihop:unknown",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 27957,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 132,
      "text": "### Evidence inconclusive\n\nA final timeout without per-leg tests cannot identify which hop failed.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:pivot-multihop:action",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 27419,
      "width": 900,
      "height": 228,
      "text": "### Procedure entry — full sequence in the note\n\n```text\nKali -> tunnel A -> PIVOT_A -> tunnel B -> PIVOT_B -> INTERNAL_HOST:PORT\n```\n\n[[notes/pivoting.md#pivot-multihop|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:pivot-multihop:next-0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 27737,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Discover pivot interfaces, routes and internal service context\n\n**When:** A foothold exposes an interface/subnet or a loopback-only service\n\n**Still required:** A usable pivot process/identity and explicit scope; both forward and return directions must be understood\n\n**Discover pivot interfaces, routes and internal service context — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:pivot-multihop:next-1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 28044,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Build the callback and delivery routes separately from the attack route\n\n**When:** A pivoted exploit reaches its target but its shell/download cannot return\n\n**Still required:** Target-to-listener/download-server path, correct advertised address and compatible reverse listener/forward\n\n**Build the callback and delivery routes separately from the attack route — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:pivot-multihop:next-2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 28375,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Match route, destination service and effective authorization\n\n**When:** A credential appears valid but the destination's usable access is unknown\n\n**Still required:** Real source-to-service route, correct identity context and protocol-specific execution/logon rights\n\n[[tracks/09 Active Directory.canvas|Match route, destination service and effective authorization → 09 Active Directory]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:pivot-dns-tunnel:start",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 70,
      "y": 29006,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 250,
      "text": "## Conditional: tunnel through controlled DNS infrastructure\n\nDNS is an available carrier while simpler permitted routes are unavailable",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:pivot-dns-tunnel:discover",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 570,
      "y": 28966,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 180,
      "text": "### Discover\n\n```text\ndig DOMAIN NS\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:pivot-dns-tunnel:interpret",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1500,
      "y": 28946,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### What the output establishes\n\nDelegation is an infrastructure prerequisite; an NS record alone does not prove ownership or an operational tunnel.",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:pivot-dns-tunnel:validate",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1500,
      "y": 29192,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Missing prerequisite\n\nConfirm authorized control, resolver path, compatible client/server/runtime and supported intended operation.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:pivot-dns-tunnel:enabled",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 28896,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Condition confirmed\n\nThe controlled carrier and required application operation work: use this constrained fallback.\n\n**Verify:** Verify the actual carrier and intended forwarded action; retain delegation and connectivity prerequisites.\n\n[[notes/pivoting.md#pivot-dns-tunnel|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:pivot-dns-tunnel:ruledout",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 29237,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 132,
      "text": "### Condition disproved here\n\nNo approved domain/control or required DNS path exists: reject this design.",
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:pivot-dns-tunnel:unknown",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 29434,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 132,
      "text": "### Evidence inconclusive\n\nAn isolated DNS callback does not establish a stable tunnel or full route.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:pivot-dns-tunnel:action",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 28896,
      "width": 900,
      "height": 228,
      "text": "### Procedure entry — full sequence in the note\n\n```bash\ndnscat2-server --secret=SHARED_SECRET TUNNEL_DOMAIN\n```\n\n[[notes/pivoting.md#pivot-dns-tunnel|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:pivot-dns-tunnel:next-0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 29214,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Relay a single TCP service through a fixed forward\n\n**When:** One reachable pivot can connect to one internal TCP destination\n\n**Still required:** A bindable pivot listener, source-to-listener access and pivot-to-destination connectivity\n\n**Relay a single TCP service through a fixed forward — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:pivot-dns-tunnel:next-1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 29521,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Discover pivot interfaces, routes and internal service context\n\n**When:** A foothold exposes an interface/subnet or a loopback-only service\n\n**Still required:** A usable pivot process/identity and explicit scope; both forward and return directions must be understood\n\n**Discover pivot interfaces, routes and internal service context — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:pivot-dns-tunnel:next-2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 29828,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Maintain state and select the next evidence-producing test\n\n**When:** Several hosts, identities, routes or competing hypotheses need coordination\n\n**Still required:** Explicit scope/objective and a record of observations, unknowns and available capabilities\n\n[[tracks/12 Evidence and Reporting.canvas|Maintain state and select the next evidence-producing test → 12 Evidence and Reporting]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "track-title",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 0,
      "width": 2300,
      "height": 270,
      "color": "5",
      "text": "# 10 Pivoting\n\nAll workflows, commands, result interpretations and method connections for this track are on this canvas. Embedded notes contain the complete procedures and variants.\n\n[[START.canvas|Choose another track]]\n\nCross-track results link directly to the receiving track."
    }
